  "caveats": [
    "Every ranking pair is two rows of one (ligand, cell) group under two metals, so 100% support is a property of the protocol, not a measurement. There is no unsupported stratum to report and none can be constructed without new data.",
    "The intervals are Wilson intervals on TPR and TNR, propagated to balanced accuracy. They are not ligand-clustered: the stored artifacts keep only the per-pair aggregate, not the per-pair rows, so the resampling unit is unavailable without refitting. Wilson intervals will be narrower than a cluster bootstrap because ligands repeat across pairs.",
    "Rh-Ru has 16 pairs with 1 negative, so its TNR is 0 or 1 and its balanced accuracy of 0.5 carries no information. It is reported, not used.",
    "The sample-size curve assumes the observed TPR/TNR and positive rate hold at larger n. It is a design calculation, not a projection of achievable accuracy."
  ]
